course: dictionary
lesson: 12851
title: Endurance: keeping going
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Endurance is a noun. It means the ability to keep going through something long, hard or painful without giving up. «Running a marathon needs great endurance.» A marathon is very long, so the runner has to keep going even when tired.
explain: In sport, endurance means you can keep up effort for a long time. This is also called stamina. «Building endurance takes weeks of training, a little more each day.» Swimmers and cyclists train for endurance so they can go further.
explain: Endurance can also describe things, not just people. «The old boots showed great endurance and lasted ten years of muddy walks.» Here it means the boots lasted a long time without breaking. Check the words around it to see which meaning fits.
fact: Endurance means the ability to keep going through something long, hard or painful.
fact: In sport, endurance is the same as stamina: keeping up effort for a long time.
fact: «A test of endurance» is something long or hard enough to show how strong you are.
fact: Endurance is an uncountable noun, so we say «great endurance», not «an endurance».
fact: The explorer Ernest Shackleton named his ship Endurance.
exercise: «The runner showed great endurance in the last mile of the race.» What does endurance mean here? | Being very fast at the start | Being very tall | *Being able to keep going through something long and hard | Being able to sing loudly
exercise: «Sam trained every day to build his endurance for the swim.» What is endurance in this sentence? | A kind of cold water | *Stamina, keeping up effort for a long time | Wearing a swimming cap | Winning a medal at once
exercise: Ruby says endurance means the same as speed. Is she right? | No, endurance is a colour | *No, endurance is about lasting a long time, not about being fast | Yes, endurance and speed mean exactly the same thing | Yes, but only in swimming races
test: «The old bridge showed endurance, standing strong for two hundred years.» In this sentence endurance means... | Being very loud | Being very colourful | *The ability to last a long time without breaking
test: Which phrase means something that is too hard to bear? | Build endurance | *Beyond endurance | Endurance race
exam: Which sentence uses endurance correctly? | The children endurance the long hike. | *Her endurance helped her finish the long hike. | The hike was endurance and green.
